{"ts":"2026-08-02T21:05:06.550Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"5e676b30ed4e8585ecf5ff9e","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-1tns7o"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The N-branch convergence property is proven only over the field class that cannot diverge: the randomized suite varies one union collection and compares it sorted"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"tests/fuzz/project-boundaries.fuzz.spec.ts:219 is the property that carries the convergence claim: 'converges randomized N-branch item appends independent of merge order'. It builds each branch by setting metadata.tags to a single generated tag, folds the branches with mergeItemDocuments in original and reversed order, and asserts converge(tags).sort() equals converge(reverse(tags)).sort(). Every element of that construction lands inside ITEM_UNION_COLLECTION_FIELDS, the eleven collections that merge by element identity and therefore cannot conflict; the assertion then sorts away even the ordering. No scalar field is varied, ours and theirs are never swapped, and the merged document is never compared as a whole. The conflict policy the merge actually implements — scalar three-way resolved toward the preferred side — has no convergence property at all. This is a gate-scope defect and is filed separately from the product behaviour it fails to cover, following the pm-wlqxg3/pm-m0yjtg precedent."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["convergence","gate","merge","property-testing"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-02T21:05:06.550Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-02T21:05:06.550Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The convergence property varies at least one scalar metadata field and the body in addition to union collections, and compares the whole merged document rather than a single field; The property asserts both application-order independence and merge-direction independence, exercising each branch pair as ours and as theirs; A deliberate regression that makes any union field direction-dependent, and a deliberate regression in the scalar path, each fail the suite; Every field class the merge distinguishes — union collection, latest-timestamp, scalar three-way — is named in the property and covered by at least one generated case, and adding a new field class without extending the property fails a conformance check"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"A property suite that can only pass is not evidence; pm-2sbj8p names this suite as the acceptance evidence for the convergence model."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"The convergence property covers every field class the merge policy distinguishes, and a direction-dependent scalar fails it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The ADR that must choose the convergence model is blocked on evidence this suite is supposed to supply."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-33cw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"921c0b384ba6ed2516701a56da494acc201b005ab6aa52991c881c66989ad547","message":""}
